        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.122,
            0.293,
            0.145
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.153,
            0.847,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "1. Find, without dividing, whether the following numbers are divisible by 9. (i) 123   (ii) 405 (iii) 8888   (iv) 93547 (v) 358095"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.218,
            0.597,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Only the number in (ii) is divisible by 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.247,
            0.685,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": "2. Find the smallest multiple of 9 with no odd digits."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.274,
            0.447,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Even digits are 2, 4, 6, 8."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.299,
            0.847,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": "Since sum is 9 which is odd and cannot be formed by adding even numbers. We have smallest possible sum of digits is 18. Try forming numbers with digits 2, 4, 6, 8 to get the sum 18. The combination of even digits that sum is 18 is (2, 8, 8) Arranging these digits 288 is the smallest number that is divisible by 9, with no odd digits."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.446,
            0.749,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "3. Find the multiple of 9 that is closest to the number 6000."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.473,
            0.264,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** 6003."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.502,
            0.845,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": "4. How many multiples of 9 are there between the numbers 4300 and 4400?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.547,
            0.241,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** 11"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.577,
            0.288,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 128**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.605,
            0.846,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "If this difference is 11 or a multiple of 11, what does that say about the remainder obtained when the number is divisible by 11?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.656,
            0.255,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Zero"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.692,
            0.845,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": "？ Using this shortcut, find out whether the following numbers are divisible by 11. Further, find the remainder if the number is not divisible by 11. (i) 158   (ii) 841   (iii) 481   (iv) 5529   (v) 90904   (vi) 857076 **Ans.** (i) 4 (ii) 5 (iii) 8 (iv) 7 (v) Divisible by 11 (vi) Divisible by 11 **Page No. 129**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
